  "user_request_original": "Design a planar multilayer dielectric anti-reflection coating for silicon substrate. Incidence medium: air. Substrate: semi-infinite silicon (si). Wavelength bands: 1260-1360 nm and 1530-1565 nm. Incidence angle: 0 degrees. Polarization: unpolarized. Stack topology: 8 layers total, alternating Ta2O5 (Gao) and SiO2 (Lemarchand) starting with Ta2O5 (Gao) adjacent to air. Layer sequence: air | Ta2O5 (Gao) (layer 0) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) (layer 1) | Ta2O5 (Gao) (layer 2) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) (layer 3) | Ta2O5 (Gao) (layer 4) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) (layer 5) | Ta2O5 (Gao) (layer 6) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) (layer 7) | si. Optimization constraints: layers 0 and 7 locked at thicknesses from iteration 04 best candidate (layer 0: 185.61 nm, layer 7: 33.20 nm). Layers 1-6 optimizable with initial seed centered at 55 nm quasi-symmetric distribution. Perturbation step size: ±5 nm maximum. All layer thicknesses must remain within 20-400 nm bounds. Objective: minimize average reflectance across both wavelength bands simultaneously, report transmittance into silicon substrate. Use gradient-based thickness optimization.",
